#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Culture - Arts" tvg-id="980321555" tvg-name="In 1928‚ the novel Belle de Jour by Joseph Kessel shocked bourgeois France. The story of Sévèrine‚ a happily married well-to-do woman who lives out her sexual fantasies by prostituting herself in a brothel‚ caused an even bigger stir in 1967 with Luis Buñuel's film adaptation starring Catherine Deneuve.<br/>From 22.10.2025 14:26" tvg-country="Germany" tvg-language="English" channel-id="ARTE.EN",Belle du Jour - The Dark Side of a French Classic (Originalversion mit Untertitel) (22.10.2025)
