#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Discovery - Travel" tvg-id="1027800677" tvg-name="A world tour of traditional care‚ with Bernard Fontanille‚ French emergency doctor. Given privileged access to a sumo 'stable'‚ where sumos live and train‚ Bernard meets Tomoyuki Inui. Thanks to his expertise in Chinese medicine and osteopathy‚ Tomoyuki has dedicated his professional life to creating customised treatments for his sumo clients.<br/>From 22.02.2016 15:48" tvg-country="Germany" tvg-language="English" channel-id="ARTE.EN",Medicines of the World: Japan - The Secrets of the Sumo (Originalversion mit Untertitel) (22.02.2016)
https://arteptweb-a.akamaihd.net/am/ptweb/053000/053900/053966-006-A_SQ_0_VOF-STE%5BANG%5D_10570801_MP4-2200_AMM-PTWEB-100904022579627_2ildw1Db2Kx.mp4
#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Discovery - Travel" tvg-id="547857174" tvg-name="The Australian rural outback is notoriously dangerous and difficult to reach. As the saying goes: 'Anything can kill you in Australia!' And so if anything goes wrong several hours away from civilisation‚ emergency help must come by air. Bernard Fontanille visits the Sunshine Coast to meet the elite doctor-paramedic teams that come to the rescue.<br/>From 01.03.2016 15:43" tvg-country="Germany" tvg-language="English" channel-id="ARTE.EN",Medicines of the World - Air Care in Australia (Originalversion mit Untertitel) (01.03.2016)
https://arteptweb-a.akamaihd.net/am/ptweb/053000/053900/053966-005-A_SQ_0_VOF-STE%5BANG%5D_10570752_MP4-2200_AMM-PTWEB-100904312745838_2ildu1Db2Kx.mp4
#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Discovery - Travel" tvg-id="650065217" tvg-name="Yucatan peninsula‚ Mexico‚ is the cradle of Mayan civilization‚ which is three thousand years old. Bernard Fontanille‚ a Western emergency doctor‚ meets with Don Galo‚ a traditional doctor who belongs to the highest category of caregivers‚ H'men. Both healers and priests use the Mayan gods‚ and are responsible for the health of the land and the people who cultivate it.<br/>From 25.02.2016 16:37" tvg-country="Germany" tvg-language="English" channel-id="ARTE.EN",Medicines of the World - Mayan Healers (Originalversion mit Untertitel) (25.02.2016)
https://arteptweb-a.akamaihd.net/am/ptweb/053000/053900/053966-004-A_SQ_0_VOF-STE%5BANG%5D_10569281_MP4-2200_AMM-PTWEB-100903190574146_2ijxB1DWqC5.mp4
#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Discovery - Travel" tvg-id="350490522" tvg-name="In late 2013 a Franco-Cameroonian team made an incredible discovery. A painkiller molecule‚ already developed in the laboratory‚ actually occurs naturally in the roots of a shrub: the African peach tree and traditional healers have always known about this remedy.<br/>From 08.03.2016 15:50" tvg-country="Germany" tvg-language="English" channel-id="ARTE.EN",Medicines of the World - Cameroon's Pain Killing Tree (Originalversion mit Untertitel) (08.03.2016)
https://arteptweb-a.akamaihd.net/am/ptweb/053000/053900/053966-007-A_SQ_0_VOF-STE%5BANG%5D_10574662_MP4-2200_AMM-PTWEB-100903578586552_2ipJF1DfEKp.mp4
#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Discovery - Travel" tvg-id="279744263" tvg-name="Nestled between Zambia‚ Tanzania and Mozambique‚ the little known Malawi is one of the smallest countries in Africa. Far from the myths of sorcery that are omnipresent in the country‚ modern day healers are eager to innovate their practice and integrate elements of modern medicine. Kachepa Bulumeni and his assistant Martha watch over the health of isolated communities.<br/>From 18.03.2016 16:30" tvg-country="Germany" tvg-language="English" channel-id="ARTE.EN",Medicines of the World: Malawi - Healers of the Hills (Originalversion mit Untertitel) (18.03.2016)
